### What each group proves

| Check | Property established |
| --- | --- |
| arithmetic sanity | Pure-JS curve matches published secp256k1 vectors (`2G`, `3G`), `n*G = O`, codec round-trips. |
| Feldman VSS | Shares satisfy the committed polynomial; any `t` Lagrange-combine to the dealer secret and `PK`. |
| FROST signing | A `t`-of-`n` aggregate `(R, z)` satisfies ordinary Schnorr `z*G = R + c*PK`, i.e. indistinguishable from a single-party signature. 25 randomized 2-of-3 runs all verify. |
| commitment consistency | A share computed against a tampered commitment, or under a different commitment list (equivocation), is rejected because `rho_i` and `R_i` are re-derived from the recorded list. |
| known-DL abort | Under a binding-factor-less coordinator, colluders set `D_2=-D_1, E_2=-E_1` to force `R=O`; `aggregateNonce` returns identity and `signShare`/`aggregate` throw **before** revealing a share. The companion test removes the guard and shows `x = z/c` recovers the dealer secret while the signature still verifies. The same cancellation fails with the binding factor enabled. |

